Day 2 – SELECT, WHERE, ORDER BY, DISTINCT
=================================================================================================================================================================================
📘 Theory
=====================================================================================================================================================================
SELECT Statement

Used to retrieve data from tables.

SELECT column1, column2 FROM table_name;
SELECT * FROM table_name; -- all columns

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHERE Clause (filters rows)

Comparison operators: =, <>, >, <, >=, <=

Logical operators: AND, OR, NOT

Pattern matching: LIKE 'A%', LIKE '%x', LIKE '_a%'

Range: BETWEEN ... AND ...

Membership: IN (..,..)

DISTINCT

Removes duplicate values.

ORDER BY

Sorts results by one/multiple columns.

Default = ASC (ascending). Use DESC for descending.

SELECT * FROM Employee ORDER BY salary DESC;


LIMIT / TOP

LIMIT n → MySQL/Postgres

TOP n → SQL Server
